WEBVTT

00:00.150 --> 00:02.045
The first picture of a black hole.

00:02.745 --> 00:11.433
Far beyond our own galaxy, in a galaxy called M87, is a black hole with the mass of six and a half billion Suns.

00:11.883 --> 00:18.517
This is the first picture ever made of one, taken by eight radio telescopes working together.

00:18.967 --> 00:24.272
The dark middle is its shadow, and it is far wider than our whole Solar System.
